WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.619 --> 00:00:02.869
(laughing)

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:15.669
- Hi guys, I'm Avi and
I love one-liner jokes.

00:00:15.669 --> 00:00:17.640
Here's one that I came up with:

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:18.628
I know I should love myself

00:00:18.628 --> 00:00:19.749
before I love anyone else,

00:00:19.749 --> 00:00:22.211
but me and myself are seeing
other people right now.

00:00:22.211 --> 00:00:24.331
(laugh track laughter)

00:00:24.331 --> 00:00:25.400
I thought I'd challenge my friends

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:27.867
to come up with one-liners in 24 hours.

00:00:27.867 --> 00:00:29.468
- I feel like I can tell
if something's funny

00:00:29.468 --> 00:00:31.068
but I'm personally not funny.

00:00:31.068 --> 00:00:32.491
I don't think anyone thinks

00:00:32.491 --> 00:00:34.491
"Kane, he's hilarious."

00:00:34.491 --> 00:00:37.419
- I think I can be funny when
I'm not supposed to be funny

00:00:37.419 --> 00:00:40.419
but if somebody asks me to tell a joke

00:00:40.419 --> 00:00:42.199
or I'm supposed to make people laugh

00:00:42.199 --> 00:00:44.639
then it just all collapses and I fail.

00:00:44.639 --> 00:00:47.447
- I'm hoping to write one funny joke

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:49.449
and just remember that for
the rest of my life today.

00:00:49.449 --> 00:00:50.796
- There has to be a science to this.

00:00:50.796 --> 00:00:53.748
- Hi, I'm Doctor Sal
Attardo, I'm a linguist.

00:00:53.748 --> 00:00:56.820
And I specialize in the
linguistics of humor.

00:00:56.820 --> 00:00:59.620
There is something called
the Principle of Cooperation

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:03.569
and basically the idea is
that when you communicate,

00:01:03.569 --> 00:01:05.902
you're following some rules.

00:01:06.828 --> 00:01:09.676
All jokes have to violate in some aspect,

00:01:09.676 --> 00:01:11.099
the Principle of Cooperation.

00:01:11.099 --> 00:01:14.569
Take for example, the
joke by Dmitri Martin.

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:16.188
- I think the worst time
to have a heart attack

00:01:16.188 --> 00:01:18.438
is during a game of charades.

00:01:18.438 --> 00:01:20.559
(laughter)

00:01:20.559 --> 00:01:22.060
- When you reach the word "charades",

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:24.980
you realize that in fact, the
speaker wasn't cooperating.

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:27.039
When you get that, you get

00:01:27.039 --> 00:01:30.007
one of the basic foundations of humor.

00:01:30.007 --> 00:01:31.827
- To help Kane and Fernando, I brought in

00:01:31.827 --> 00:01:33.518
a stand up comedy teacher.

00:01:33.518 --> 00:01:34.518
- All right.

00:01:35.708 --> 00:01:36.573
- Come on in.

00:01:36.573 --> 00:01:37.406
- Okay.

00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:40.522
There is no the way to do it.

00:01:40.522 --> 00:01:41.642
Don't try to be funny.

00:01:41.642 --> 00:01:43.034
Try to be honest.

00:01:43.034 --> 00:01:46.034
Have it come from some place in you.

00:01:48.224 --> 00:01:49.493
All right guys, that's our class.

00:01:49.493 --> 00:01:50.853
- Wait, is this the whole lesson?

00:01:50.853 --> 00:01:52.062
Wait, what.

00:01:52.062 --> 00:01:54.729
(clock ticking)

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:57.931
This is so much harder
than I thought it'd be.

00:01:57.931 --> 00:01:59.752
- I have one and a half jokes.

00:01:59.752 --> 00:02:01.733
- So I'm about to test the jokes

00:02:01.733 --> 00:02:03.333
for the very first time on Juan.

00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:04.632
I used to be embarrassed about

00:02:04.632 --> 00:02:08.024
how my boyfriend and I
met, but then I realized--

00:02:08.024 --> 00:02:08.882
- All right, I'm done.

00:02:08.882 --> 00:02:11.543
- But then I realized
some people get used to

00:02:11.543 --> 00:02:13.704
(laughing)

00:02:13.704 --> 00:02:17.186
- I'm the one who's supposed
to be laughing here.

00:02:17.186 --> 00:02:18.272
- I can't believe I'm the person

00:02:18.272 --> 00:02:21.122
that starts laughing
before I can finish a joke.

00:02:21.122 --> 00:02:23.390
- I was trying to write these jokes.

00:02:23.390 --> 00:02:25.082
I needed five, but I could only come up

00:02:25.082 --> 00:02:26.482
with one and a half.

00:02:26.482 --> 00:02:27.730
- [Fernando] Okay guys, so just please

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.049
be gentle, I have one joke.

00:02:29.049 --> 00:02:32.421
So you know how I'm like a
Mexican immigrant, right?

00:02:32.421 --> 00:02:33.701
Something that's really been bugging me

00:02:33.701 --> 00:02:35.850
for a while is that
Donald Trump was saying

00:02:35.850 --> 00:02:39.082
that we are rapists and we are criminals

00:02:39.082 --> 00:02:41.450
and we're here to steal people's jobs.

00:02:41.450 --> 00:02:42.283
The job he probably
thinks we're getting is

00:02:42.283 --> 00:02:45.661
joining the Republican Party
and running for Congress.

00:02:45.661 --> 00:02:49.200
- (laughing) Wait, no.

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:50.668
(laughing)

00:02:50.668 --> 00:02:51.501
- [Fernando] Get it?

00:02:51.501 --> 00:02:52.334
Okay.

00:02:53.405 --> 00:02:54.869
- I didn't get it until the last second,

00:02:54.869 --> 00:02:57.322
I was like "Oh, oh."

00:02:57.322 --> 00:02:59.173
- I don't know, I would
give it like a six.

00:02:59.173 --> 00:03:01.063
- Verbal validation from Asian parents

00:03:01.063 --> 00:03:02.511
is like being constipated.

00:03:02.511 --> 00:03:04.431
It takes blood, sweat, and tears just

00:03:04.431 --> 00:03:06.303
to get the little bit out.

00:03:06.303 --> 00:03:08.522
- (laughs) It's so true.

00:03:08.522 --> 00:03:09.813
- I used to be embarrassed to say

00:03:09.813 --> 00:03:11.343
my boyfriend and I met online,

00:03:11.343 --> 00:03:13.260
but hey, sometimes you get furniture

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:16.435
off Craigslist, sometimes
you get a boyfriend.

00:03:16.435 --> 00:03:17.293
- Yeah.

00:03:17.293 --> 00:03:18.126
- Nah.

00:03:19.051 --> 00:03:20.605
- That's a no go.

00:03:20.605 --> 00:03:22.855
(laughing)

00:03:24.115 --> 00:03:25.435
- So I finished all the one-liners

00:03:25.435 --> 00:03:26.875
and told all the people.

00:03:26.875 --> 00:03:30.062
I got a lot of silent
stares and confusion.

00:03:30.062 --> 00:03:31.795
But you know, that's okay.

00:03:31.795 --> 00:03:35.128
Not everyone can do what I did in a day.

00:03:36.104 --> 00:03:37.794
- I think if anything, this made me

00:03:37.794 --> 00:03:41.410
understand how difficult it
is to consciously be funny.

00:03:41.410 --> 00:03:44.200
- Even though I got a
lot of awkward silences,

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.851
I almost didn't care
because I was just proud

00:03:46.851 --> 00:03:51.018
that I was able to go
through with it and perform.

